>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `split_ss`

``` hol4
simpLib.split_ss : ssfrag
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Splits datatype case expressions and `split` rules during simplification.

`split_ss` is the fragment `"split"`. Its looper `"splitter"` applies
`splitLib.SPLIT_TAC` with the theorems of the current theory and its
ancestors that carry the `split` attribute (`Theorem name[split]: ...`,
which rejects malformed rules) and the split rules of every datatype
whose case constant occurs fully applied in the goal. The fragment also
rewrites `(b ==> t) /\ (~b ==> t)` to `t`.

`ExclX "split:thy$name"` disables the attribute rule `thy$name` for one
call, and `ExclX "case:ty"` the rules of datatype `ty`; see
[`simpLib.ExclX`](#simpLib.ExclX).

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>> SIMP_TAC (bool_ss ++ simpLib.split_ss) []
     ([], “P (if b then 1 else 2) : bool”) c;
>> SIMP_TAC (bool_ss ++ simpLib.split_ss) [ExclX "case:bool"]
     ([], “P (if b then 1 else 2) : bool”) c;
```

### See also

[`splitLib.SPLIT_TAC`](#splitLib.SPLIT_TAC),
[`simpLib.add_split`](#simpLib.add_split),
[`simpLib.del_split`](#simpLib.del_split),
[`simpLib.Split`](#simpLib.Split).
